        "text": "A Practical Reverse Shell Using USB Rubber Ducky\nand PowerShell\nThis chapter ends with a great recipe for reverse shells against Windows operating\nsystems, using PowerShell. This scripting language was invented by Microsoft\nas an equivalent to Bash in Linux OS. Before you learn how to take advantage\nof this behavior in practice, here are the steps used in this scenario:\n1.I Generate a PowerShell reverse shell using SET.\n2.I Start a listener on the Kali host.\n3.I Host the .ps1 PowerShell file on the Kali web server.\n118\nChapter 5 I Social Engineering Attacks\n4. Switch to the Windows host and run PowerShell in administrative mode.\n5.I Execute a command that will download and execute the .ps1 script host\non the Kali VM.\n6.I Check that you have a reverse shell on the Windows host.\n7.I Re-create the PowerShell scene using the USB Rubber Ducky.",
